-- A dead let-binding whose right-hand side has no measurable distribution.
-- `Uniform * Uniform` is a product of two independent random variables: the
-- modality engine types it Bottom, so none of IRCompiler's Apply arms that
-- require a measurable argument pType applies. But `x` never occurs in the
-- body, so the argument's law integrates out to 1 and the program is just
-- `Uniform` -- which is what ModalityInfer says too, since a directly-applied
-- lambda takes its pType from the *body*. Before investigation
-- 60_toIRInference-apply-gap this crashed the compiler with a bare
-- "This instance of apply is not yet implemented".
main = let x = Uniform * Uniform in Uniform
